Adriaan de Groot wrote:
> I hate trappers. They eat all my favorite pets, like Archons, and just
> now a Xorn (while in Vlad's tower). This was odd, because when the trapper
> swallowed the Xorn, the Xorn was phased into a wall, and the trapper 
> ended up in the wall where the Xorn had just been. Can we invent some
> kind of metaphysical explanation for how the trapper managed to fit
> _around_ the Xorn to swallow it, while the Xorn was surrounded by rock?

The same reason why Mojo ends up in the castle wall after hitting a 
phasing xorn. Xorns don't walk through walls by phasing out themselves 
(this way they wouldn't be able to carry stuff) but by creating 'air 
bubbles' in solid matter. This bubble is big enough for the xorn to move 
freely in combat. Displacing rock is quite slow so a tight-fitting phase 
bubble would make the xorn unable to defend itself, also spherical (or 
ellipsoid) bubbles are easier to create than irregularly shaped ones. So 
what happened was, the trapper engulfed the xorn (obviously it was small 
enough to fit between xorn and wall) and digested it. The moment the 
xorn died the phase bubble collapsed, leaving the trapper in solid rock.

